---
// Anatomy of the review that appears before a signature.
// A written description of the screen's structure. Not a screenshot, and every
// value shown is invented.
---

<svg
  class="u-dg"
  viewBox="0 0 640 542"
  role="img"
  aria-labelledby="dg-rev-t dg-rev-d"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
>
  <title id="dg-rev-t">The order in which a signature request is presented, top to bottom</title>
  <desc id="dg-rev-d">
    The approval screen is stacked in a fixed order and is read from the top. First,
    anything blocking: a check that failed hard, which cannot be clicked through
    and leaves the approve control disabled. Second, the impact summary: what
    leaves your wallet, what returns, the resulting net change, and any assets
    touched, each carrying a confidence mark of exact, estimated or unknown. Third,
    the overall status, which is ready, review or blocked, and which can never be
    ready while any fact is unknown. Fourth, warnings that do not block, such as
    address reputation notes and decoded risk rows. Fifth, the details: network,
    destination, the single fee statement, the full input and output list, and the
    raw transaction. Reject sits beside approve at the same size, and rejecting
    costs nothing. A footnote states the two rules that matter: a fact the wallet
    could not read is shown as unknown rather than rounded to zero or hidden, and a
    request that changes after you looked at it is refused rather than signed.
  </desc>

  <text class="dg-kicker" x="0" y="14">READ IT FROM THE TOP. THE ORDER IS THE ARGUMENT.</text>

  <!-- 1 blocking -->
  <rect class="dg-alert-panel" x="0.75" y="26.75" width="638.5" height="62.5" rx="3" />
  <text class="dg-kicker" x="16" y="48">1. BLOCKING</text>
  <text class="dg-sm" x="16" y="72">A check that failed hard. Approve stays disabled. This is not a warning you can click past.</text>
  <text class="dg-mono dg-dim" x="500" y="48">Blocked</text>

  <!-- 2 impact -->
  <rect class="dg-panel" x="0.75" y="98.75" width="638.5" height="122.5" rx="3" />
  <text class="dg-kicker" x="16" y="120">2. IMPACT</text>
  <text class="dg-sm" x="16" y="146">Leaves your wallet</text>
  <text class="dg-mono" x="300" y="146">0.03450000 BTC</text>
  <text class="dg-mono dg-dim" x="500" y="146">EXACT</text>
  <text class="dg-sm" x="16" y="170">Comes back to you</text>
  <text class="dg-mono" x="300" y="170">0.01446152 BTC</text>
  <text class="dg-mono dg-dim" x="500" y="170">EXACT</text>
  <text class="dg-sm" x="16" y="194">Token balance moved</text>
  <text class="dg-mono" x="300" y="194">250 TOKEN out</text>
  <text class="dg-mono dg-dim" x="500" y="194">ESTIMATED</text>
  <text class="dg-sm dg-dim" x="16" y="214">Every line carries its own confidence. The screen takes the worst one.</text>

  <!-- 3 status -->
  <rect class="dg-panel" x="0.75" y="230.75" width="638.5" height="62.5" rx="3" />
  <text class="dg-kicker" x="16" y="252">3. STATUS</text>
  <text class="dg-sm" x="16" y="276">Ready, Review, or Blocked. It can never read Ready while any fact is unknown.</text>

  <!-- 4 warnings -->
  <rect class="dg-panel" x="0.75" y="302.75" width="638.5" height="62.5" rx="3" />
  <text class="dg-kicker" x="16" y="324">4. WARNINGS</text>
  <text class="dg-sm" x="16" y="348">Things worth knowing that do not block: address reputation, decoded risk rows, advisories.</text>

  <!-- 5 details -->
  <rect class="dg-panel" x="0.75" y="374.75" width="638.5" height="106.5" rx="3" />
  <text class="dg-kicker" x="16" y="396">5. DETAILS</text>
  <text class="dg-sm dg-dim" x="16" y="420">Network and account</text>
  <text class="dg-sm dg-dim" x="16" y="440">Destination, marked external when it is not yours</text>
  <text class="dg-sm dg-dim" x="16" y="460">The fee, stated once, in one place</text>
  <text class="dg-sm dg-dim" x="340" y="420">Every input and every output</text>
  <text class="dg-sm dg-dim" x="340" y="440">Which inputs are protected</text>
  <text class="dg-sm dg-dim" x="340" y="460">The raw transaction, copyable</text>

  <!-- footer rules -->
  <rect class="dg-panel-2" x="0.75" y="490.75" width="638.5" height="50.5" rx="3" />
  <text class="dg-sm" x="16" y="514">
    Reject sits beside Approve, the same size. Rejecting costs nothing and can always be repeated.
  </text>
  <text class="dg-sm dg-alert-text" x="16" y="534">A request that changes after you looked at it is refused, not signed.</text>
</svg>
